# Courtois-NeuroMod: [mario3 subdataset](https://github.com/courtois-neuromod/mario3)

The [Courtois project on Neural Modelling (Courtois NeuroMod)](https://www.cneuromod.ca/) aims at training artificial neural networks using extensive experimental data on individual human brain activity and behaviour.

Participants played levels of Mario3 while functional data being acquired in the MRI scanner . A extensive description can be found [here](https://docs.cneuromod.ca/en/latest/DATASETS.html#mario3).

This subdataset is organized following the [brain imaging data structure (BIDS)](https://bids.neuroimaging.io/) (including extensions in development) and contains:
- [x] [raw neuroimaging data](https://docs.cneuromod.ca/en/latest/MRI.html#functional-sequences)
- [x] behavioral variables in event files
- [ ] physiological data
  - [ ] ECG
  - [ ] pulse (photoplethysmography)
  - [ ] respiration
  - [ ] skin conductance (electro-dermal activity)
- [ ] eyetracking gaze and pupillometry

*(unchecked are collected data which have not yet been integrated in the dataset)*

Courtois NeuroMod data are [freely shared with the scientific community](https://docs.cneuromod.ca/en/latest/ACCESS.html) to advance research at the interface of neuroscience and artificial intelligence. Access to to the data is based on a registered access model, see the Courtois NeuroMod website for more information. Redistribution of data outside of the Courtois NeuroMod data bank is prohibited.


## Annotated game events

`sub-*/ses-*/func/*_desc-annotated_events.tsv` carry the game events aligned to the fMRI
runs: one `gym-retro_game` row per repetition (one `.bk2` replay), and inside it the
player's actions, deaths, power-up states, enemies on screen, level completion and the
screens shown (title card, death sequence, end-of-level sequence, transitions). They are
generated from the replays by `code/annotations/generate_annotations.py`, a thin front end
over the shared [`videogames_utils.events`](https://github.com/courtois-neuromod/videogames_utils)
package. The vocabulary is documented in `task-mario3_events.json` (BIDS sidecar),
`code/annotations/README.md` (every event this game may emit, with its row count and
accuracy notes) and the cross-game
[`docs/EVENT_REFERENCE.md`](https://github.com/courtois-neuromod/videogames_utils/blob/main/docs/EVENT_REFERENCE.md).
Per-repetition metadata (`phase`, `IndexInRun`, `IndexGlobal`, `IndexLevel`, `Outcome`)
is in `gamelogs/*_summary.json`.

